Title: Mary Had a Little Lamb
Credit: Adapted from the nursery rhyme by
Author: Sarah Josepha Hale (public domain)
Source: Mary Had a Little Lamb
Draft date: 8/20/2026

FADE IN:

EXT. COUNTRY LANE - DAY

A painted rail fence, meadow flowers. MARY, a small girl in a blue
dress, walks with a white LAMB trotting at her heel.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
Mary had a little lamb,
Its fleece was white as snow.

MARY
Come along, little lamb.

The lamb noses her hand. They walk on together.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
And everywhere that Mary went,
The lamb was sure to go.

INT. SCHOOLROOM - DAY

Rows of wooden desks. CHILDREN giggle as the lamb clatters in
behind Mary. The TEACHER looks up from the chalkboard.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
It followed her to school one day,
Which was against the rule.

CHILDREN
A lamb! A lamb at school!

NARRATOR (V.O.)
It made the children laugh and play
To see a lamb at school.

TEACHER
Out it goes — lambs belong in the meadow.

EXT. SCHOOLHOUSE - DAY

The teacher shoos the lamb out the door. It circles, then settles
by the step, watching the door.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
And so the teacher turned it out,
But still it lingered near.

The lamb waits patiently. The school bell rings. Mary runs out and
the lamb bounds to her, laying its head on her arm.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
And waited patiently about
Till Mary did appear.

INT. SCHOOLROOM - DAY

The children crowd the doorway, watching Mary and the lamb below.

CHILDREN
Why does the lamb love Mary so?

TEACHER
Why, Mary loves the lamb, you know.

NARRATOR (V.O.)
And you each gentle animal
In confidence may bind,
And make them follow at your call,
If you are always kind.

FADE OUT.
